<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibrahim Adil Shah I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1558">1558</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibrahim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shah">Adil Shah</a> I ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shahi-dynasty">Bijapur Sultanate</a> from 1534 to 1558, after the brief reign of his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallu-adil-shah">Mallu Adil Shah</a>. Breaking with his predecessors, he adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni Islam</a>, favoured the Deccani nobility over Persian immigrants and replaced Persian with local languages in revenue records. His reign was taken up by wars with Vijayanagara and the neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-sultanates">Deccan sultanates</a>, especially <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmadnagar">Ahmadnagar</a>.</p></div>
